>In article <14838@netnews.upenn.edu> song@grad1.cis.upenn.edu.UUCP (Mitchell So
>ng) writes:
>:I would like to make a request for a monk character in nethack.
>
>The Samurai is sort of like this already, except he kicks instead of using
>his hands.  But if this *were* to be implemented, something would need to
>be done to counterbalance the fact that he can't possibly have his weapon
>rusted, damaged by a scroll, lost, cursed, etc. 

What happens when a monk hits a cockatrice with his "main" weapon, or how
about a creature that can only hit by magical weapons. (I'm not sure if this
is true in nethack but it is in AD&D)  How effective is the monk's punch/kick
when he is wearing armor.  In AD&D he's not allowed to wear any armor (well
body armor and shield anyway.)  The same could apply to the monk's abilities.
If he's wearing body armor, shield, or a helmet (and maybe gloves) he can't 
use some of his unique abilities.  But a monk does seem to fit into nethack 
somewhat.  At certain levels, he could get intrinsic poison resistance, 
intrinsic speed, and maybe others.  There are probably many ways to limit the
monk, don't give up on it.  Oh, also, if anyone is going to look into the 
AD&D monk, look at the new revised monk, the article is in  Best of Dragon IV 
